  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 330 AM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\n- Dry and Mild with Morning Fog\n\nEnsembles continue to lend high confidence in tranquil and warmer\nthan normal conditions through the weekend. A sharpening upper\nlevel ridge over the central CONUS will reinforce a sprawling high\npressure anticyclone in the low levels across the Great Lakes,\nmigrating toward the Northeast. There is increasing ensemble \nspread and thus lower confidence in high temperatures starting on\nMonday and extending through the week, and highs may plausibly be\nanywhere in the 50s or 60s. This will depend on the magnitude of\nnorthern stream troughing that occurs over south-central Canada\nand the Great Lakes, and the southward extent which cooler air \nmay reach. Ensemble members also diverge into clusters regarding \nthe the potential for a recovery of warmer air around the middle\nof the week. So, next week is relatively unsettled.\n\nAreas of fog are likely to develop each of the next few mornings,\nas they have the past couple mornings. The REFS handled the\ngeneral location of the Wednesday morning fog threat in Mid \nMichigan fairly well. For this Thursday morning it has been \nsuggesting areas of overnight fog mainly between Muskegon and \nLudington, which has so far been the case, and patchy fog may \ndevelop elsewhere around daybreak. Tonight into Friday morning, \nwith the surface high centered north of Lake Huron, a flow of \nrelatively moist air off Lake Huron will spread into Mid Michigan \nduring the late evening, setting up fog potential first near \nUS-127 and spreading west toward US-131 areas around daybreak \nFriday.\n\n- Chances for Rain Return Next Week\n\nThe chance for precipitation is basically nil until about Tuesday\nor Wednesday next week, and even so is far from settled. Any\nindividual model solutions producing heavy rain or strong winds \nthe middle of next week are outliers. The potential for a \nsignificant autumn storm system -- even with the unsettled \nevolution of the northern stream -- is remarkably low for this\npoint in the season.",
